        <h2 id="what-is-pseo">What is Programmatic SEO?</h2>

        <p>
          Programmatic SEO is the practice of creating hundreds or thousands of SEO-optimized pages automatically using templates and data. 
          Instead of manually writing each page, you build a system that generates pages dynamically based on structured data.
        </p>

        <p>
          Think about how Zillow has millions of pages for every property, street, and neighborhood. Or how TripAdvisor has pages for every hotel, 
          restaurant, and attraction. These weren't manually created—they were programmatically generated using a template and database.
        </p>

        <h3>The Core Components of Programmatic SEO</h3>

        <ol>
          <li><strong>Template Pages:</strong> A single, well-optimized template that can be populated with different data points</li>
          <li><strong>Structured Data:</strong> A database of information (locations, products, services, etc.) that populates the templates</li>
          <li><strong>URL Structure:</strong> A scalable URL pattern that search engines can easily crawl and index</li>
          <li><strong>Unique Value:</strong> Each generated page must provide genuine value, not just keyword-stuffed templates</li>
          <li><strong>Internal Linking:</strong> Automated cross-linking between related pages to distribute link equity</li>
        </ol>

        <p>
          The magic of PSEO isn't just about creating lots of pages—it's about creating pages that match specific search intent at scale. 
          When someone searches for "plumber in Austin Texas," your programmatically generated page for that exact location should appear.
        </p>

