        <h3>Step 2: Build Your Template</h3>

        <p>
          Your template is the blueprint for every page you'll generate. It should include:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>H1 Tag:</strong> Dynamic with location/modifier (e.g., "[Service] in [City], [State]")</li>
          <li><strong>Unique Intro:</strong> Context-specific introduction (use city data, local stats)</li>
          <li><strong>Data Display:</strong> Show your core offering (listings, products, services)</li>
          <li><strong>Local Information:</strong> Relevant details about the location/modifier</li>
          <li><strong>FAQs:</strong> Common questions specific to that variation</li>
          <li><strong>Internal Links:</strong> Related pages (nearby locations, similar services)</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="highlight">
          <p>
            <strong>⚡ Pro Tip:</strong> Google can detect thin, low-quality programmatic pages. Each page MUST have unique, valuable content. 
            Use local data APIs, statistics, and custom-written snippets to differentiate your pages.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h3>Step 3: Scale Your Page Generation</h3>

        <p>
          Once your template is proven, it's time to scale. Modern PSEO implementations use:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>Static Site Generators:</strong> Tools like Next.js, Gatsby, or Astro to pre-render pages</li>
          <li><strong>Database-Driven:</strong> PostgreSQL or MongoDB to store your data points</li>
          <li><strong>Build Scripts:</strong> Automated scripts that generate pages from your data</li>
          <li><strong>Incremental Builds:</strong> Only regenerate changed pages to maintain speed</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          The technical implementation varies, but the principle remains: one template + structured data = thousands of optimized pages.
        </p>

        <h3>Step 4: Optimize for Indexation</h3>

        <p>
          Creating pages is only half the battle—you need Google to find and index them. Best practices include:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Submit XML sitemaps with all your generated pages</li>
          <li>Build strong internal linking to help Googlebot discover pages</li>
          <li>Start with high-value pages before scaling to everything</li>
          <li>Monitor indexation in Google Search Console</li>
          <li>Use strategic pagination to avoid overwhelming crawlers</li>
        </ul>

